--TEST--
a case's read is counted above the case and the enum written in front of it above the enum, so one read raises two counts and the case nothing reads says so, `rule:ide/five-features-are-one-reference-index`
--FILE--
<?nvs
enum Suit {
    case Hearts;
    case Spades;
}
var $s = Suit::Hearts;
--REQUEST--
codeLens
--EXPECT--
2:6 1 reference
3:10 1 reference
4:10 no references
